{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Ensemble Methods Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Decision Stump (Base Learner)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code in `code/ensembles.py` implements everything from scratch. We start with a decision stump: a tree with a single split."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class DecisionStump:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.feature_idx = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.threshold = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.polarity = 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.alpha = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y, weights):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n_samples, n_features = X.shape"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best_error = float(\"inf\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for f in range(n_features):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            thresholds = np.unique(X[:, f])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for thresh in thresholds:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                for polarity in [1, -1]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    pred = np.ones(n_samples)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    pred[polarity * X[:, f] < polarity * thresh] = -1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    error = np.sum(weights[pred != y])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    if error < best_error:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        best_error = error"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        self.feature_idx = f"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        self.threshold = thresh"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                        self.polarity = polarity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = X.shape[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = np.ones(n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        idx = self.polarity * X[:, self.feature_idx] < self.polarity * self.threshold"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred[idx] = -1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return pred"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: AdaBoost from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class AdaBoostScratch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_estimators=50):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_estimators = n_estimators"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.stumps = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.alphas = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = X.shape[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        weights = np.full(n, 1 / n)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(self.n_estimators):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            stump = DecisionStump()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            stump.fit(X, y, weights)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pred = stump.predict(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            err = np.sum(weights[pred != y])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            err = np.clip(err, 1e-10, 1 - 1e-10)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            alpha = 0.5 * np.log((1 - err) / err)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            weights *= np.exp(-alpha * y * pred)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            weights /= weights.sum()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            stump.alpha = alpha"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.stumps.append(stump)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.alphas.append(alpha)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total = sum(a * s.predict(X) for a, s in zip(self.alphas, self.stumps))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return np.sign(total)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Gradient Boosting from Scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class GradientBoostingScratch:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_estimators=100, learning_rate=0.1, max_depth=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_estimators = n_estimators"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.lr = learning_rate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_depth = max_depth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.trees = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.initial_pred = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.initial_pred = np.mean(y)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        current_pred = np.full(len(y), self.initial_pred)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(self.n_estimators):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            residuals = y - current_pred"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tree = SimpleRegressionTree(max_depth=self.max_depth)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tree.fit(X, residuals)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            update = tree.predict(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            current_pred += self.lr * update"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.trees.append(tree)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pred = np.full(X.shape[0], self.initial_pred)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for tree in self.trees:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            pred += self.lr * tree.predict(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return pred"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Compare against sklearn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The code verifies that our from-scratch implementations produce similar accuracy to sklearn's `AdaBoostClassifier` and `GradientBoostingClassifier`, and compares all methods side by side."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. Modify the AdaBoost implementation to track training accuracy after each round. Plot accuracy vs. number of estimators. When does it converge?\n\n2. Implement a random forest from scratch by adding random feature subsampling to the regression tree. Train 100 trees with `max_features=sqrt(n_features)` and average predictions. Compare variance reduction to a single tree.\n\n3. In the gradient boosting implementation, add early stopping: track validation loss after each round and stop when it has not improved for 10 consecutive rounds. How many trees does it actually need?\n\n4. Build a stacking ensemble with three base models (logistic regression, decision tree, k-nearest neighbors) and a logistic regression meta-learner. Use 5-fold cross-validation to generate meta-features. Compare to each base model alone.\n\n5. Run XGBoost on the same dataset with default parameters. Compare its accuracy to your from-scratch gradient boosting. Time both. How large is the speed difference?"
      ]
    }
